/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Satellite images play a crucial role in various applications such as environmental monitoring, disaster management, and urban planning. However, atmospheric conditions, particularly haze, significantly degrade the quality of these images, reducing visibility and affecting the accuracy of downstream tasks like object detection and land classification. Traditional image dehazing techniques, including histogram equalization and dark channel prior \(DCP\), often fail to generalize across different atmospheric conditions and may introduce artifacts or excessive smoothing.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
